summary:
  The search preview's retry ladder ignores a park, so a parked audition is
  played again by a late directory reply.

history:
  The same shape as 37, one subsystem over. A relay-backed audition CAN be
  parked — that is the whole point of the FLAC listener's pause — but the
  preview ladder runs on its own identity (_previewSeq / _previewUrl) rather
  than on the standing order, because an audition never raises _wantsPlaying.
  So the shared recovery gate does not apply here and the park had nowhere to
  live: every rung passed its identity check and played. The rung guard is
  where it belongs, since all three rungs already go through it. Found
  2026-09-18 while closing 37: the same complaint on #13 had a second road
  through the search results, and closing one without the other would have
  meant answering the reporter too early.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
              return root._previewSeq === pvSeq && root._previewUrl === pvKey
                     && !root._tsPaused;

replace:
              return root._previewSeq === pvSeq && root._previewUrl === pvKey;

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_every_automatic_recovery_road_asks_the_intent_not_the_state.
  Line-neutral.
